From d495c65cac83f52c23519074e30bd326a6b5c58d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FVOCI <150913557+fvoci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:04:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(collab): move a live document inside its room so held
 edits are saved or never acknowledged (#71)

The move checkpoint answered before the move transaction, and after the
commit the room kept accepting edits until the next permission recheck.
The periodic store acknowledged those edits (the browser drops its
draft), yet when the target workspace had realtime off and the editor
could not write there, the room's last snapshot had no author and the
edits stayed only as a pending state nothing recovers.

- Command::Move runs checkpoint -> move transaction -> post-commit work
  inside the room, like restore. Messages that arrive meanwhile wait in
  the room queue. If the move does not happen (preview changed, error,
  caller gone) the room carries on and accepts them as usual.
- After the commit the room applies only messages received before the
  commit instant, writes a revision in the new place (the mover stands
  in when no editor can write there), acknowledges it, closes every
  connection with 4409 and ends. If no revision can be written it closes
  the connections first and only then stores the state.
- Without a room, a per-document moving guard keeps a new room from
  opening during the move (4503, reconnect later).
- Shutdown and the recheck realtime-off close no longer acknowledge
  edits they could not save as a revision.
- The 200 body carries the document including the room's last revision.

Tests: edits_between_the_checkpoint_and_the_move_are_kept_or_never_acknowledged,
edits_held_by_a_move_that_does_not_happen_are_accepted,
a_move_closes_the_room_after_saving_its_edits,
no_room_opens_while_a_document_moves; the moved-room test now expects
4409 at the move and a new room in the target workspace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
